const tips = [
  { title: "Resolve Saint Killingham and Your Leader in Either Order", cards: [leader, killinghamBlack, sleeptids], paragraphs: [
    "Saint Gunko requires careful management of your Trash, board space, and effect-resolution order. Some interactions let you recover additional Characters or avoid mistakes that can cost you a game.",
    "When you play OP18-083 Saint Killingham from your Trash during your turn, you can resolve its On Play effect and your Leader effect in either order.",
    "If Sleeptids is not yet in your Trash, resolve your Leader effect first to draw two cards and send one to your Trash. You may put OP18-093 Sleeptids there before resolving Saint Killingham's effect and playing it right away.",
    "This interaction is especially useful when your Trash does not yet contain all the pieces you need."
  ]},
  { title: "Use Your Five Character Slots", cards: [killinghamPurple, cerberus, shamrock], paragraphs: [
    "The five-Character board limit can become restrictive, but you can also use it to return a Character to your Trash and reuse its effect.",
    "Against Red Law, one possible sequence is:",
    "1. Play OP18-064 Saint Killingham from your Trash to prevent opposing Characters from attacking.",
    "2. When your board is full, play Cerberus in place of purple Saint Killingham, which then returns to your Trash.",
    "3. Activate Cerberus to return it to your hand and give Rush, Banish, or Unblockable to Saint Shamrock.",
    "4. Use another available effect, such as Saint Gunko's Activate: Main effect or I'll Make the Call, to play purple Saint Killingham from your Trash a second time.",
    "This lets you reuse its control effect without keeping all your Characters on the field unnecessarily."
  ]},
  { title: "Plan Your Board Space Before Black Saint Killingham", cards: [killinghamBlack, sleeptids], paragraphs: [
    "Plan ahead for the spaces you need before playing black Saint Killingham: its effect can play Sleeptids, so you need two available spaces if you want to keep both Characters on the field."
  ]},
  { title: "Know the Different K.O. Effects on Saint Killingham", cards: [killinghamPurple, killinghamBlack], paragraphs: [
    "Both Saint Killinghams can return from your Trash after a K.O., but they use different resources.",
    "Purple Saint Killingham uses DON!! −1 to return to the field. Black Saint Killingham sends two cards from your hand to your Trash to return to the field.",
    "Before using black Saint Killingham's effect, make sure the two cards you discard will not be more useful for defending your Leader or preparing your next turn."
  ]},
  { title: "Protect Your Characters from Non-K.O. Removal", cards: [zoro], paragraphs: [
    "These effects do not activate when a Character leaves the field without being K.O.'d, including when it is returned to the bottom of the deck.",
    "Roronoa Zoro can protect your Characters from opposing effects that would remove them from the field by placing three cards from your Trash under your deck.",
    "This protection uses resources from your Trash, so use it on Characters whose presence on your board really matters.",
    "Characters that can return after being K.O.'d are still vulnerable to effects that return them to the hand, put them on the bottom of the deck, or send them directly to the Trash. Against decks such as Buggy, Spandam, or Rocks, having Zoro on the field is very important.",
    "Also watch for effects that disable your Blockers, including Teach at 10 DON!!. A pile of Sleeptids does not guarantee you can defend your Leader if your opponent can stop you from using them. In those situations, prioritize Characters that apply immediate pressure or directly prevent opposing attacks."
  ]},
  { title: "Reuse Cerberus on Saint Shamrock", cards: [cerberus, shamrock], paragraphs: [
    "You can replay Cerberus several times during the same turn to stack different effects on Saint Shamrock.",
    "Rush + Banish lets you attack immediately while sending Life cards hit directly to the Trash without activating their Triggers. Rush + Unblockable threatens the opposing Leader right away, without letting Blockers intercept the attack. You can also stack all three effects if you have enough DON!!.",
    "Do not automatically spend your resources to add multiple effects. Rush alone may be enough if your goal is to remove a rested opposing Character."
  ]},
  { title: "Choose Between Black and Purple Saint Killingham", cards: [killinghamBlack, killinghamPurple], paragraphs: [
    "Black Saint Killingham can play Sleeptids, but it is not always the best option.",
    "In some situations, purple Saint Killingham can prevent two opposing Characters from attacking and protect your Leader more effectively. This is especially useful when the opponent has several attackers or one Character that represents a major threat.",
    "On the other hand, if you need a Blocker to defend against a big attack next turn, black Saint Killingham may be preferable.",
    "Choose based on the attacks you need to stop, not simply on how many Characters you can play."
  ]},
  { title: "Use Mamaragan to Create Attacks", cards: [mamaragan], paragraphs: [
    "Mamaragan can create attack opportunities that would not otherwise be available.",
    "Against OP13 Sabo, you can use Mamaragan to rest Ripley, then use Saint Shamrock with Rush to attack and remove it.",
    "You can then reserve your other Characters' attacks for opposing threats that are already rested. This sequence lets you clear several Characters in the same turn instead of focusing all your attacks on the opposing Leader."
  ]}
];

const renderText = (text) => text.split(/(\*\*.*?\*\*)/g);
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero guide-hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="hero-tags"><span class="hero-chip">Deck Guide</span><span class="hero-chip hero-chip-accent">OP18 Format</span></div><h1>{title}</h1><p class="hero-intro">{heroIntro}</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#curve">Game Plan &amp; Curve</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#matchups">Matchups</a><a class="btn btn-secondary btn-card-list" href="/cards-list/OP18/">Card List OP18</a></div></div><div class="guide-icon"><img src={guideIcon} alt="Saint Gunko OP18 deck guide icon" loading="eager" /></div></div></section>
  <div class="container article-stack">
    <section id="decklist" class="glow-block"><div class="decklist-title-row"><h2>Decklist</h2><button class="btn btn-primary copy-sim-button" type="button" data-copy-sim={simDeckCode}>Copy for Sim</button></div><div class="deck-grid">{decklist.map((entry) => <button class="deck-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(entry.img)} alt={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} loading="lazy"/><div class="deck-info"><b class="deck-count">{entry.count}x</b><span>{entry.name}<small class="deck-code">{entry.code}</small><small class="deck-role">{entry.role}</small></span></div></button>)}</div></section>
    <section id="mulligan" class="glow-block"><h2>Mulligan</h2>{mulliganIntro.map((text) => <p>{text}</p>)}<div class="content-list">{mulligan.map((item) => <article class={`content-item ${item.cards.length ? "has-cards" : "text-only"} ${item.title === "Cards to Set Up in Your Trash" ? "trash-setup-item" : ""}`}><h3>{item.title}</h3>{item.cards.length > 0 && <div class="card-row">{item.cards.map((entry) => <button class="mini-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(entry.img)} alt={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} loading="lazy"/></button>)}</div>}<div class="paragraphs">{item.paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{renderText(text).map((part) => part.startsWith("**") && part.endsWith("**") ? <strong>{part.slice(2,-2)}</strong> : part)}</p>)}</div></article>)}</div></section>
    <section id="curve" class="glow-block"><h2>Curve Guide</h2><p>Saint Gunko aims to fill your Trash quickly so you can play black Saint Killingham + Sleeptids, then develop your board with Saint Shamrock and Saint Gunko at 10 DON!!.</p><p>The deck works when going first, but except in certain matchups, it is better to go second.</p>{[["Going First", curveFirst], ["Going Second", curveSecond]].map(([heading, curve]) => <div class="curve-block"><h3>{heading}</h3>{curve.map((item) => <article class="curve-item"><strong>{item.title}</strong><div class="curve-content"><div class={`card-set ${item.cards.length === 4 ? "four" : ""} ${item.cards.length === 3 ? "three" : ""} ${item.connectors?.length ? "connected" : ""} ${item.cardGroups ? "option-rows" : ""}`}>{item.cardGroups ? item.cardGroups.map((group, groupIndex) => <div class="card-option-row">{groupIndex > 0 && <span class="connector option-prefix">OR</span>}{group.map((entry, index) => <>{index > 0 && <span class="connector">+</span>}<button class="mini-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(entry.img)} alt={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} loading="lazy"/></button></>)}</div>) : item.cards.map((entry, index) => <>{index > 0 && item.connectors?.[index - 1] && <span class={`connector ${item.optionRows && item.connectors[index - 1] === "OR" ? "option-break" : ""}`}>{item.connectors[index - 1]}</span>}<button class="mini-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(entry.img)} alt={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} loading="lazy"/></button>{item.cardSuffixes?.[index] && <span class="card-count-label">{item.cardSuffixes[index]}</span>}</>)}</div><div class="curve-note">{item.paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{renderText(text).map((part) => part.startsWith("**") && part.endsWith("**") ? <strong>{part.slice(2,-2)}</strong> : part)}</p>)}</div></div></article>)}</div>)}</section>
    <section id="tech-cards" class="glow-block"><h2>Tech Cards</h2><p>This version of Saint Gunko uses several cards to strengthen its defense, protect its Characters, and manage opposing threats. Cerberus, Sleeptids, Sugar, Zoro, and Mamaragan each have a specific role, though some slots can be adapted to the metagame.</p><div class="content-list"><h3 class="tech-subtitle">Tech Cards in the Decklist</h3>{techCards.map((item, index) => <>{index === 10 && <h3 class="tech-subtitle">Other Possible Tech Cards</h3>}<article class={`tech-card ${item.card ? "" : "text-only"}`}>{item.card && <button class="mini-card tech-card-image" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={item.card.img} data-name={`${item.card.code} ${item.card.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(item.card.img)} alt={`${item.card.code} ${item.card.name}`} loading="lazy"/></button>}<h3>{item.title}</h3><div class="paragraphs">{item.paragraphs.map((text, paragraphIndex) => <>{paragraphIndex === 1 && item.bullets && <ul class="tech-bullets">{item.bullets.map((bullet) => <li>{renderText(bullet).map((part) => part.startsWith("**") && part.endsWith("**") ? <strong>{part.slice(2,-2)}</strong> : part)}</li>)}</ul>}<p>{renderText(text).map((part) => part.startsWith("**") && part.endsWith("**") ? <strong>{part.slice(2,-2)}</strong> : part)}</p></>)}</div></article></>)}</div></section>
    <section id="matchups" class="glow-block"><h2>Matchup Analysis</h2><p class="matchup-stats-link">See Gunko&apos;s win rates when going first or second in <a href="/meta-analysis/Saint-Gunko-op18-stats-OP18-Format/"><strong>OP18 Saint Gunko 1st/2nd Win Rates.</strong></a></p><p>Saint Gunko has several favorable matchups thanks to its ability to regularly play Characters from the Trash. Very aggressive decks and those that can remove your Characters without K.O.'ing them can be more difficult to manage.</p><p>The deck is generally better when going second.</p>{matchupGroups.map((group) => <div class="matchup-group"><h3>{group.title}</h3><div class="content-list">{group.items.map((item) => <article class="content-item matchup-card"><div class="matchup-heading"><button class="mini-card matchup-leader-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={item.leader.img} data-name={`${item.leader.code} ${item.leader.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(item.leader.img)} alt={`${item.leader.code} ${item.leader.name} Leader`} loading="lazy"/></button><div class="matchup-title-stack"><h3>{item.title}</h3>{item.rating && <span class={`matchup-rating-badge rating-${item.ratingTone}`}>{item.rating}</span>}</div></div>{item.paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{text}</p>)}</article>)}</div></div>)}<div class="matchup-group"><article class="content-item matchup-card"><div class="matchup-heading"><button class="mini-card matchup-leader-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={matchupSummaryLeaders.luffyOp13.img} data-name={`${matchupSummaryLeaders.luffyOp13.code} ${matchupSummaryLeaders.luffyOp13.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(matchupSummaryLeaders.luffyOp13.img)} alt="Monkey D. Luffy OP13 Leader card" loading="lazy"/></button><div class="matchup-title-stack"><h3>Matchup to Reevaluate: Red/Green Luffy</h3></div></div>{matchupReevaluation.map((text) => <p>{text}</p>)}</article></div></section>
    <section id="matchup-ratings" class="glow-block matchup-overview"><div class="section-header"><div><h2>Matchups</h2><p>Quick OP18 matchup spread for Saint Gunko.</p></div></div><div class="matchup-overview-grid">{matchupSummaryGroups.map((group) => <div class="matchup-overview-group"><div class={`matchup-overview-badge overview-badge-${group.tone}`}><span class="matchup-overview-icon">{group.icon}</span><span>{group.label}</span></div><div class="matchup-overview-list">{group.cards.map((entry) => <button class="matchup-overview-entry" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} data-code={entry.code}><img src={getOptimizedAssetUrl(matchupSummaryIcons[entry.code] ?? entry.img)} alt={`${entry.name} Leader`} loading="lazy"/><span>{entry.name}</span></button>)}</div></div>)}</div></section>
    <section id="tips" class="glow-block"><h2>Tips</h2><div class="content-list">{tips.map((item) => <article class="content-item has-cards"><h3>{item.title}</h3><div class="card-row">{item.cards.map((entry) => <button class="mini-card" type="button" data-card-preview data-full={entry.img} data-name={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`}><img src={getCardThumbnail(entry.img)} alt={`${entry.code} ${entry.name}`} loading="lazy"/></button>)}</div><div class="paragraphs">{item.paragraphs.map((text) => <p>{renderText(text).map((part) => part.startsWith("**") && part.endsWith("**") ? <strong>{part.slice(2, -2)}</strong> : part)}</p>)}</div></article>)}</div></section>

  </div>
  <div class="card-modal" data-modal aria-hidden="true"><div class="card-modal-inner" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Card preview"><button class="modal-close" type="button" data-close>Close</button><img src="" alt="" data-modal-image/></div></div>
</MainLayout>

<script>
  const modal = document.querySelector("[data-modal]"); const modalImage = document.querySelector("[data-modal-image]");
  const closeModal = () => { modal?.classList.remove("is-open"); modal?.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true"); document.body.style.overflow = ""; };
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-card-preview]").forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => { if (!modal || !modalImage) return; modalImage.src = button.dataset.full || ""; modalImage.alt = button.dataset.name || "Card preview"; modal.classList.add("is-open"); modal.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "false"); document.body.style.overflow = "hidden"; }));
  document.querySelector("[data-close]")?.addEventListener("click", closeModal); modal?.addEventListener("click", (event) => { if (event.target === modal) closeModal(); });
  document.querySelector("[data-copy-sim]")?.addEventListener("click", async (event) => { const button = event.currentTarget; try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copySim); const previous = button.textContent; button.textContent = "Copied"; window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = previous; }, 1800); } catch { button.textContent = "Copy failed"; } });
</script>

